          <span class="section-tag">THE ARCHIVE</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">THE LIFE OF <span>CRISTIANO RONALDO</span></h2>
          <p class="section-subtitle">
            Cristiano Ronaldo dos Santos Aveiro is a Portuguese professional footballer widely recognized for his extraordinary goalscoring record, athletic ability, and enduring longevity at the highest level of football.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Bio Overview Card -->
        <div class="bio-overview-card reveal-fade-up">
          <div class="bio-overview-text">
            <h3>Born to Make History</h3>
            <p>
              Born on <strong>5 February 1985</strong> in Funchal, Madeira, Portugal, Ronaldo was raised in the working-class neighbourhood of Santo António. From barefoot games on concrete alleys to world dominance, his ascent is the definitive modern tale of obsessive discipline, physical transformation, and uncompromising belief.
            </p>
            <div class="bio-highlight-pill">
              <span>CR7 • 20+ Years at World Peak Level</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="bio-profile-stats">
            <div class="profile-stat-box">
              <span class="stat-box-title">Full Name</span>
              <span class="stat-box-value">C. Ronaldo dos Santos Aveiro</span>
            </div>
            <div class="profile-stat-box">
              <span class="stat-box-title">Birthplace</span>
              <span class="stat-box-value">Funchal, Madeira, Portugal</span>
            </div>
            <div class="profile-stat-box">
              <span class="stat-box-title">Position</span>
              <span class="stat-box-value">Forward / Winger</span>
            </div>
            <div class="profile-stat-box">
              <span class="stat-box-title">Squad Number</span>
              <span class="stat-box-value">#7 (Iconic)</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Timeline-Style Biography -->
        <div class="bio-timeline-wrapper">

          <!-- 1. Early Life in Madeira -->
          <article class="bio-item reveal-fade-up">
            <div class="bio-node"></div>
            <div class="bio-card">
              <span class="bio-card-era">1985 — 2001</span>
              <h3 class="bio-card-title">Early Life in Madeira</h3>
              <p class="bio-card-text">
                Ronaldo developed an unrelenting passion for football from an early age in Funchal. He began his youth career playing for local side <strong>Andorinha</strong>, where his father served as kit man, before moving to <strong>CD Nacional</strong>. His precocious technical speed caught the eyes of scouts across mainland Portugal.
              </p>
              <ul class="bio-meta-list">
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">Funchal, Madeira</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">CF Andorinha</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">CD Nacional</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="bio-media">
              <img src="assets/images/madeira.jpg" alt="Madeira CR7 Museum in Funchal" loading="lazy">
              <div class="bio-media-badge">Funchal, Madeira</div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- 2. Sporting CP -->
          <article class="bio-item reveal-fade-up">
            <div class="bio-node"></div>
            <div class="bio-card">
              <span class="bio-card-era">2001 — 2003</span>
              <h3 class="bio-card-title">Sporting CP Academy Breakthrough</h3>
              <p class="bio-card-text">
                At just 12 years old, Ronaldo moved alone to Lisbon to join Sporting CP's famed youth academy. He became the only player in club history to represent the under-16, under-17, under-18, B-team, and first team in a single season. In August 2003, his mesmerizing display against Manchester United in the inauguration of the Estádio José Alvalade sealed his transfer to England.
              </p>
              <ul class="bio-meta-list">
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">First-team Debut at 17</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">Supertaça Cândido de Oliveira</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">31 Appearances</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="bio-media">
              <img src="assets/images/young-cr7.jpg" alt="Young Cristiano Ronaldo Breakthrough" loading="lazy">
              <div class="bio-media-badge">Sporting CP to Man Utd</div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- 3. Manchester United First Spell -->
          <article class="bio-item reveal-fade-up">
            <div class="bio-node"></div>
            <div class="bio-card">
              <span class="bio-card-era">2003 — 2009</span>
              <h3 class="bio-card-title">Manchester United: The Making of an Icon</h3>
              <p class="bio-card-text">
                Handed the iconic number 7 shirt by Sir Alex Ferguson, Ronaldo evolved from a dazzling step-over winger into a ruthless goal-machine. In 2007–08, he scored 42 goals across all competitions, leading United to the Premier League and UEFA Champions League double, earning him his maiden <strong>Ballon d'Or</strong> and FIFA World Player of the Year awards.
              </p>
              <ul class="bio-meta-list">
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">2008 UEFA Champions League</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">3x Premier League Titles</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">2008 Ballon d'Or</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">118 Goals in 292 Apps</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="bio-media">
              <img src="assets/images/manchester-united-classic.jpg" alt="Cristiano Ronaldo at Manchester United" loading="lazy">
              <div class="bio-media-badge">Old Trafford Glory</div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- 4. Real Madrid -->
          <article class="bio-item reveal-fade-up">
            <div class="bio-node"></div>
            <div class="bio-card">
              <span class="bio-card-era">2009 — 2018</span>
              <h3 class="bio-card-title">Real Madrid: The Galáctico Era</h3>
              <p class="bio-card-text">
                Transferred to Real Madrid in a then-world record £80 million deal before 80,000 fans at the Santiago Bernabéu. Over nine seasons, Ronaldo shattered every scoring record in club history, netting an astonishing <strong>450 goals in 438 matches</strong> (1.03 goals per game). He spearheaded Real Madrid to four Champions League titles—including the historic three-peat (2016, 2017, 2018)—and captured four more Ballon d'Or trophies.
              </p>
              <ul class="bio-meta-list">
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">All-Time Top Scorer: 450 Goals</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">4x UEFA Champions League</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">4x Ballon d'Or Awards</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">2x La Liga Titles</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="bio-media">
              <img src="assets/images/real-madrid.jpg" alt="Cristiano Ronaldo at Real Madrid" loading="lazy">
              <div class="bio-media-badge">Santiago Bernabéu Legend</div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- 5. Juventus -->
          <article class="bio-item reveal-fade-up">
            <div class="bio-node"></div>
            <div class="bio-card">
              <span class="bio-card-era">2018 — 2021</span>
              <h3 class="bio-card-title">Juventus: Dominance in Italy</h3>
              <p class="bio-card-text">
                Seeking a new challenge in Serie A, Ronaldo signed with Juventus and became the fastest player in club history to reach 100 goals (in just 131 games). He won two consecutive Serie A titles, the Coppa Italia, and two Supercoppa Italiana titles, also winning the Serie A Capocannoniere top-scorer award.
              </p>
              <ul class="bio-meta-list">
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">101 Goals in 134 Matches</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">2x Serie A Titles</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">Serie A Player of the Year</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">Capocannoniere Winner</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="bio-media">
              <img src="assets/images/juventus.jpg" alt="Cristiano Ronaldo at Juventus" loading="lazy">
              <div class="bio-media-badge">Turin Triumph</div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- 6. Return to Manchester United -->
          <article class="bio-item reveal-fade-up">
            <div class="bio-node"></div>
            <div class="bio-card">
              <span class="bio-card-era">2021 — 2022</span>
              <h3 class="bio-card-title">Return to Manchester United</h3>
              <p class="bio-card-text">
                In August 2021, Ronaldo completed a triumphant return to Old Trafford. On his second debut, he scored twice against Newcastle United to a rapturous reception. He finished the season as Manchester United's top scorer with 24 goals across all competitions and was voted the Sir Matt Busby Player of the Year, officially passing 800 career goals.
              </p>
              <ul class="bio-meta-list">
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">24 Goals in 38 Matches</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">800th Career Goal Milestone</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">Sir Matt Busby Player of the Year</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="bio-media">
              <img src="assets/images/manchester-united-return.jpg" alt="Cristiano Ronaldo Old Trafford Return" loading="lazy">
              <div class="bio-media-badge">Old Trafford Return</div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- 7. Al Nassr -->
          <article class="bio-item reveal-fade-up">
            <div class="bio-node"></div>
            <div class="bio-card">
              <span class="bio-card-era">2023 — Present</span>
              <h3 class="bio-card-title">Al Nassr: Pioneering a New Era</h3>
              <p class="bio-card-text">
                In January 2023, Ronaldo joined Saudi Arabian club Al Nassr, catalyzing a worldwide renaissance for the Saudi Pro League. He won the Arab Club Champions Cup in 2023 and set the single-season league scoring record with 35 goals, becoming the first player in history to win top-scorer awards in four different top-flight leagues.
              </p>
              <ul class="bio-meta-list">
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">Arab Club Champions Cup</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">Saudi Pro League Golden Boot (35 Goals)</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">First to Top-Score in 4 Leagues</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="bio-media">
              <img src="assets/images/al-nassr.jpg" alt="Cristiano Ronaldo Al Nassr Era" loading="lazy">
              <div class="bio-media-badge">Al Nassr Captain</div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- 8. Portugal National Team -->
          <article class="bio-item reveal-fade-up">
            <div class="bio-node"></div>
            <div class="bio-card">
              <span class="bio-card-era">2003 — Present</span>
              <h3 class="bio-card-title">Portugal: Eternal National Icon</h3>
              <p class="bio-card-text">
                Ronaldo made his senior international debut for Portugal in August 2003 at age 18. He captained Portugal to their historic first major silverware at <strong>UEFA EURO 2016</strong> in France, followed by the inaugural <strong>2019 UEFA Nations League</strong> title. UEFA lists Ronaldo with <strong>234 appearances and 146 goals</strong> for Portugal—both all-time world records in men's international football.
              </p>
              <ul class="bio-meta-list">
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">UEFA EURO 2016 Champions</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">UEFA Nations League 2019</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">World Record 146 Goals</li>
                <li class="bio-meta-tag">World Record 234 Caps</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="bio-media">
              <img src="assets/images/portugal-nation.jpg" alt="Cristiano Ronaldo Portugal National Team" loading="lazy">
              <div class="bio-media-badge">Portugal Captain</div>
            </div>
          </article>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

